  "summary": "The code contained a critical XSS vulnerability due to improper DOM manipulation and lacked modularity. I have refactored the function to use textContent for security, decoupled the DOM dependency by passing the target element, and added JSDoc documentation to improve maintainability.",
  "fixed_code": "/**\n * Updates the page title and results header based on the 'q' URL parameter.\n * @param {HTMLElement} targetElement - The element to display the search term in.\n */\nfunction showSearchTerm(targetElement) {\n    const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);\n    const term = params.get(\"q\") || \"\";\n    if (targetElement) {\n        targetElement.textContent = \"Results for \" + term;\n    }\n    document.title = \"Search Results\";\n}\n\ndocument.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", () => {\n    showSearchTerm(document.getElementById(\"results-title\"));\n});"
}
